# downloaded + extracted data and the built warehouse — never commit these (heavy, regenerable via
# setup.sh). Keyed by extension, NOT `data/`, so the ontology's own source under data/datasets/ and
# data/lookups/ stays tracked.
*.7z
*.parquet
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# macOS / editor cruft
.DS_Store

# build outputs / tooling — the article site now lives in meaning-as-code-articles
site/
site.zip
.wrangler/
__pycache__/

# The compile record: derived, regenerated on every projection, and machine-specific — it carries the
# operator who ran it and the raw stdout of wrapped gates, absolute paths and all. The framework
# gitignores it for the same reason. Read it locally; it is not a committed artifact.
compile.json
**/compile.json

# The ontology lock-disarm marker. It is the OPERATOR's, it is created by hand, and it must
# never travel: committed, it would arrive disarmed in every clone. Ignored so that a
# `git add -A` in a bundle where the operator has unlocked cannot carry it in.
.ontology-unlocked
